# Patch: Symforce-generated fp32 FULL_OPENCV kernels (42 new files) plus the 4 regenerated aggregates under generated/f32 (symforce 0.12.0, clang-format 21.1.2). Not hand-editable.
# Problem: stock CASPAR 4.2.0 skips FULL_OPENCV observations ("unsupported camera model"); 12 parameters do not fit a tunable calib in shared memory.
# Base:    colmap/colmap be5e29168d4aff238409d60424812df66aac919f (tag 4.2.0) + add-opencv-fisheye-caspar-adapter.patch + add-opencv-fisheye-generated-f32.patch
# Branch:  caspar-full-opencv @ 0cc0355f, on top of caspar-opencv-fisheye @ c03b1f38 (the fork the fisheye patches come from)
# Pattern: upstream COLMAP PR #4657 (fixed-calibration THIN_PRISM_FISHEYE): only fixed-intrinsics / fixed-sensor factors, calib as constant sequential data.
# Applied: rattler-build source.patches in recipes/colmap-src/recipe.yaml (examples-monorepo), after the fisheye patches.
# Checked: every patched file is hashed in patches/SHA256SUMS, verified by the build.
# Provenance: patches/PROVENANCE.md (generator command, inputs, versions).

diff --git a/src/thirdparty/Symforce-Caspar/generated/f32/caspar_mappings.cu b/src/thirdparty/Symforce-Caspar/generated/f32/caspar_mappings.cu
